# Cloudflare Pages headers (the origin since the 2026-08-02 cutover — .htaccess is dead here).
# Security baseline per docs/optimization-backlog.md §12.1 and docs/ux-cro-security.md §5.
# HSTS deliberately WITHOUT includeSubDomains (mail/webmail subdomains not guaranteed HTTPS)
# and WITHOUT preload (near-irreversible — owner's call, docs/business-facts.md §F).
#
# CSP is REPORT-ONLY. It shipped 2026-08-24 before any third-party script existed, and was widened
# for the tag manager in the same commit that added it (2026-08-30) — that rule stands: a script and
# the directive that allows it land together, never after.
#   'unsafe-inline' in style-src: Next emits inline styles; removing it costs more than it returns.
#   'unsafe-inline' in script-src is STRUCTURAL under output: "export" and cannot be removed. Next
#   streams the RSC flight payload as inline <script> tags, there is no server to mint a per-response
#   nonce, and a static file cannot carry one. A hash policy does not help either — the payload
#   changes with every build. Do NOT "tighten" this: it breaks hydration on every route.
#   connect-src: GA4 has no single endpoint. Besides www.google-analytics.com it also collects via
#   REGIONAL hosts of the form regionN.google-analytics.com. (Which region serves a given visitor is
#   Google's to decide and is not documented per country — so this does not claim one for Israel; the
#   wildcard covers them all, which is the point.) Those hosts match neither the exact
#   www.google-analytics.com nor *.analytics.google.com, which is a different registrable domain.
#   Hence *.google-analytics.com. The explicit www.google-analytics.com is kept beside it as
#   documentation of the host GA4 normally uses — note it is a subdomain the wildcard ALREADY
#   matches, not the apex, and the bare apex google-analytics.com is deliberately absent because
#   GA4 does not collect there.
#   imgquarry.com in connect-src (2026-10-12, same change as the script that needs it):
#   /assets/live.js reads the fleet status switch, https://imgquarry.com/status/fleet.json, once
#   per page view (CLAUDE.md §14). Blocked, the switch reads as unreadable and every seasonal line
#   and the card stay off — silently. The live surfaces' two inline <head> scripts are covered by
#   the existing 'unsafe-inline', /assets/live.js by 'self'.
#
# HOW TO PROMOTE IT TO ENFORCING. The previous gate — "a full week of real traffic with no
# legitimate violations" — was never executable: this header carries no report-uri and no report-to,
# so it has never collected one report and never will (optimization-backlog §12.7). Cloudflare's
# Report-Only CSP reports nowhere by itself. Use this instead; it is deterministic and needs no
# reporting endpoint.
#   1. Deploy to a Pages PREVIEW branch with the directive renamed to Content-Security-Policy
#      (enforcing). Previews already send X-Robots-Tag: noindex, so nothing is indexed.
#      ⚠️ The enforcing policy is an EDIT TO THIS FILE, and ops/deploy-site.ps1 deploys to
#      --branch main. So do it on a throwaway git branch and deploy that branch by hand with
#      wrangler (`npx wrangler pages deploy .\out --project-name thermoleak --branch csp-test`).
#      Never run the ops script while this file says enforcing, and never merge the test branch.
#   2. With the console open, walk every indexable route (28 on the 2026-10-28 build); open the
#      mobile menu, the consent banner and the seasonal card; and submit the form through to
#      /thank-you/. Each of those exercises a distinct directive — the tag manager, GA4's regional
#      endpoint, the status switch, the inline live scripts and the WhatsApp handoff — and ONLY a
#      real submit reaches /thank-you/.
#   3. Zero violations across all of it is the gate. A violation means a directive is wrong, not
#      that the console is noisy.
#   4. Only then drop "-Report-Only" here, deploy, and re-walk the same list on production.
#
# Permissions-Policy carries browsing-topics, NOT interest-cohort: FLoC was removed from Chrome, so
# that directive is inert and governs nothing. Topics replaced it and IS readable by the tag manager
# this site now loads, so Topics is the one that has to be denied.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://imgquarry.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-src https://www.googletagmanager.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

# The production pages.dev alias serves the whole site as an indexable 200 duplicate (measured
# 2026-10-19). This absolute-URL rule is Cloudflare's documented fix and matches on the request HOST,
# so thermoleak.co.il and www are untouched. Preview deployments already send noindex by default.
# After a deploy: `curl -sI https://thermoleak.pages.dev/` shows X-Robots-Tag: noindex, and
# `curl -sI https://thermoleak.co.il/` shows NO X-Robots-Tag — if it does, roll back at once.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Fingerprinted build assets are immutable by construction.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# /images/* is NOT content-hashed — hero.webp and thermoleak_logo.webp keep their names across
# deploys — so `immutable` would be wrong: a corrected image could stay cached for a year with no
# way to bust it. 30 days with normal revalidation is the right trade, and the invalidation path is
# rename-on-change (docs/performance-guidelines.md §5). Without this rule both files revalidate off
# a Cloudflare zone default that this repo does not control.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
